/* Text with the legacy color and link tags (docs/ui/AUTHORING.md "Text with
   tags and links"). The runtime registers nui-text; it builds one span per
   run from its value, through RmlUi's DOM calls, so the text is shown as
   written: never parsed as markup, translated or data-bound.

   <nui-text data-attr-value="sign.text"/>
   	a run with a color tag gets an inline color; a link run (links="on",
   	the default) is a span.nui-link with data-link, and a left press on it
   	sends nuilink (ev.link) to the element and its ancestors.
   <nui-text links="off" data-attr-value="name"/>
   	link runs show as plain runs in their color.

   The chat lines element (chat.rcss) builds its lines' runs the same way. A
   link takes the pointer in a document that otherwise does not (an overlay,
   the chat's body). The modern skins underline a hovered link; the color
   is the run's own, as legacy draws it. */

nui-text
{
	display: inline;
}
.nui-text__run
{
}
.nui-link
{
	pointer-events: auto;
}
.nui-link:hover
{
	text-decoration: underline;
}
